+Proof-of-Automation (PoA) runbook
+
+Purpose
+- Run one end-to-end automated Proof-of-Automation to validate Aegis' ability to orchestrate tokenize → train → (sim) → RT sweeps → HIL + formal closure → auditor bundle and to measure Time-to-Evidence and key KPIs.
+
+Quick start
+1. Ensure required secrets and endpoints are configured:
+   - COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, S3_UPLOAD (optional)
+2. Prepare inputs:
+   - dataset path (JSONL), invariant TLA+ file, hardware targets ("host:iface"), and scenarios file.
+3. Run:
+   COSIGN_KMS_URI=... S3_UPLOAD=... ./ops/runbooks/one_click_pofa.sh --dataset /data/train.jsonl --invariant ops/formal/specs/safety.tla --targets "ecu1:can0" --scenarios ops/av/certification/falcon_scenarios.txt --out /tmp/pofa_run
+4. After completion, collect KPI summary:
+   python3 ops/metrics/kpi_collector.py --report /tmp/pofa_run/pofa_report.json --out /tmp/pofa_kpi_summary.json
+
+Notes & expectations
+- Many steps are "best-effort" placeholders: cloud provisioning and some hardware interactions require operator action.
+- The script records a PoA report and attempts to record an evidence manifest using ops.sdk.evidence_sdk if available.
+- Use the KPI summary to measure before/after improvements; store baseline reports to compare iterations.
+
